{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group F at the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]]''' comprised [[Germany national football team|Germany]] and the [[Serbia and Montenegro national football team|Federal Republic of Yugoslavia]] of [[UEFA]], [[Iran national football team|Iran]] of the [[Asian Football Confederation]] and the [[United States national men's soccer team|United States]] from the [[CONCACAF]] region.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/98full.html |title=World Cup 1998 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

Germany and Yugoslavia both started well by beating the United States and Iran respectively. The United States was then eliminated with a match to spare after losing to Iran, while Germany drew with Yugoslavia. Iran needed to win their final game against Germany to qualify but was defeated, which meant that Yugoslavia would still have qualified even without their victory over the United States. Germany's two goals against both the United States and Iran put them top on goal difference.

